+# Detailed, varied workshop equipment and material finishes
+
+Owner request and follow-up, 2026-10-12. GW01: improve the marked workbench/tyre-rack/compressor and cabinet/shelf areas toward the car's detail quality. GW02: remove repetitive shelf stock and tool rows. GW03: add materials across the garage environment. Preserve GC06–GC28/CW13/CW15/CW16/V06/G01/R01/Q01. AAA remains an owner/device quality acceptance target.
+
+The left workshop now has a fabricated steel bench with foot pads, bolted joints, lower drawer storage, grained timber worktop, framed perforated board and shaped tools. Two spanners sit alongside a ratchet, pliers, claw hammer, measuring square, two screwdrivers and a varied socket rail. The mounted vice has a swivel base, machined/serrated jaws, spindle and sliding handle. The tyre rack has cross braces, flanged shelves, feet and bolts; complete spare wheels now use shaped alloy spokes, drilled brake details and moulded sidewall rings. This changes only garage spare wheels, not the vehicle models or their canonical geometry.
+
+The compressor is a smoothly shaded domed tank on a wheeled frame, with cooling fins, motor casing, regulator, actual pressure dial/ticks/needle, hose coil and identification plate. Curved surfaces use indexed lathed geometry with per-vertex normals, avoiding the first faceted-tank appearance. The right drawer cabinet has inset fronts, rounded recessed pulls, fasteners, side vents, kick plates, worktop/back lip and castors. Storage cases have reinforcing ribs, protective corners, lid seams, latches, hinges and open carry handles; the counter case retains its previous shelf-clearance envelope. Shelf supports now have fixing rails, slots, bolts and diagonal brackets. The original poster receives layered frame profiles and corner hardware.
+
+Shelf contents are purposefully different. The bottom shelf carries different-sized oil bottles, a handled coolant can and service tins; the middle shelf has a storage case, an open parts bin with small hardware and an open brake-parts package; the top has a woven tool bag, taped carton and differently sized tins. Positions and heights vary by collection. Repeated drawers, rack hardware and sockets remain functional sets, while the previous duplicated four-item shelf rows and repeated wrench grid are removed. There are no new inventory, repair, tuning or reward mechanics.
+
+Original cached shader finishes provide brushed alloy, powder-coated steel, cast metal, moulded plastic, rubber and woven fabric, plus a separate timber-grain shader. Painted walls, shutter panels and trophy-display backing/storage receive matching finish detail. Colour pigments use source-colour uniforms; detail attenuates with projected size and stays restrained. Roughness and surface-normal response distinguish the materials. Concrete is now mostly dielectric rather than metallic, with subtle micro-normal and roughness variation; the existing limited analytic roof-light reflection approximation remains. These are procedural opaque materials, not imported bitmap/normal-map assets or reflected room/car geometry. No external media/provider/dependency or runtime AI is added.
+
+Geometry remains prepared into the existing full-room cache/material batches; primitive and lathe meshes are shared where their shape matches. The final inspected room has **59 mesh instances, 193,038 triangles and 204,199 vertices**, all finite. This includes the architecture/trophy/roof furnishings, not just the newly marked props. Carousel environments retain their lighter prepared geometry and frozen actual car renders. Camera/zoom, roof cutaway, identical turntables, car light sweeps, local paint/dirt and the trophy-camera flow remain.
+
+Changed runtime: `game/ui/garage_environment.gd`, `garage_workshop.gd`, `garage_details.gd`, `garage_floor.gdshader`. Added `game/ui/garage_furnishings.gd`, `garage_materials.gd`, `garage_timber.gdshader`, `garage_surface_finish.gdshader` (all with UIDs). Added `game/tests/capture_garage_workshop.gd` (+UID), this document; updated `AGENTS.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+Actual commands on pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, isolated test records:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Import
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_workshop.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_workshop.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/mobile/detail'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_reference.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/overview'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_reference.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/mobile/overview'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_final_polish.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/contracts'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_carousel.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/carousel'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_car_transition.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/transition'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_studio.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_car_wash.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Doctor
+python build/checkpoint_garage_workshop_detail.py
+```
+
+Final passes: detail/variety inspection **19 Compatibility + 19 desktop Mobile/Vulkan**; reference layout/four sizes/all-five-car views **25 + 25**; roof/fixed-platform/common-camera/shelf-clearance **38**; carousel/selection/frozen cards/local cosmetics **175**, car light-sweep/zoom/cancellation **23**, exact car/glazing/render regression **80**, washing/local condition **1,402**; zero failures. Import passes. Actual car remains 64 meshes/104,558 triangles/68,996 UV vertices with exact baked/source car/glazing bytes. Final RTX 3090 Compatibility desktop diagnostic: 525.305ms cold page construction, viewport CPU median/p95 1.025/1.591ms, GPU median/p95 1.688/3.773ms. These are desktop samples, not a speedup claim or phone measurement.
+
+An initial smooth-mesh conditional assigned an untyped Array to Array[int]; corrected with PackedInt32Array. The first case-count inspection encountered auto-renamed nodes, corrected with legible unique names. After the owner's variety correction, the repeated-case count was superseded by checks for eight distinct equipment families; finite geometry, clearance, prepared batching and untouched local-condition assertions remain. A separate in-progress `BreakableProps` class import briefly blocked shared-workspace runs; the normal pinned Import registered the available class and the subsequent garage runs passed without editing that work or weakening any invariant.
+
+Inspected [complete garage](evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/overview/garage-1720.png), [left workshop](evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/detail/left-workshop.png), [varied right shelves/cabinet](evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/detail/right-workshop.png), [compressor](evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/detail/compressor.png), [vice/tools](evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12/detail/vice-tools.png), and matching Mobile views. Tight equipment views use diagnostic-only camera poses; no additional player-facing garage submenu was introduced. Clean captures use isolated local records and create no condition records. Four full-menu widths are covered: 960x540, 1280x720, 1600x720 and 1720x914.
+
+Task-only two-commit checkpoint: `build/garage_workshop_detail/checkpoint-repo`; baseline sources, scoped patch, hashes, captures and actual logs: `docs/evidence/garage-workshop-detail-2026-10-12`. Main branch/index and concurrent unrelated work are preserved. No full Validate, physics merge/regression, backend operation or deployment was performed.
+
+Doctor's final run sees an attached DN2103 Android device. **This build was not exported, installed or tested on that device.** Owner material/style acceptance and physical-device frame pacing, memory, brightness and fine-detail readability remain open. Existing future trophy population remains unchanged.
